  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116568",
      "title": "Preparing a Project For Deployment: Building It For Production",
      "lectureOrder": 315,
      "videoOrder": 298,
      "sourceHash": "d96d431c077b2c7eeac07369cb0a1c5ed257827e0506dada24dc112c6d9cff47",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 3.45,
          "en": "So how does deployment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.45,
          "end": 6.093,
          "en": "of an Angular app work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.99,
          "end": 10.74,
          "en": "Well, in the end, it's a multi-step process you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.74,
          "end": 13.59,
          "en": "And the first step, of course, is that you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.59,
          "end": 16.59,
          "en": "develop and test your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.59,
          "end": 19.38,
          "en": "Now, that's what we did throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.38,
          "end": 22.89,
          "en": "We build various Angular applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 25.29,
          "en": "and used various Angular features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.29,
          "end": 29.34,
          "en": "And of course we always also tested those applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.34,
          "end": 32.52,
          "en": "in the browser with help of that locally running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.52,
          "end": 34.74,
          "en": "development server that can be started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.74,
          "end": 37.653,
          "en": "by running npm start or ng serve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.82,
          "end": 42.42,
          "en": "And that's a development server, a web server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.42,
          "end": 46.2,
          "en": "that serves this Angular application you're building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.2,
          "end": 48.54,
          "en": "from your locally running machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.54,
          "end": 51.33,
          "en": "so from your laptop or computer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.33,
          "end": 56.01,
          "en": "And therefore only you can visit this website by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.01,
          "end": 57.18,
          "en": "no one else can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.18,
          "end": 59.58,
          "en": "unless you opened up your system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.58,
          "end": 62.4,
          "en": "to outside visitors, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.4,
          "end": 63.87,
          "en": "But even if you did,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.87,
          "end": 65.46,
          "en": "this development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.46,
          "end": 67.83,
          "en": "which has started with npm start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.83,
          "end": 70.56,
          "en": "and therefore ng serve under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.56,
          "end": 72.99,
          "en": "is actually not suited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.99,
          "end": 77.99,
          "en": "to host your production ready Angular application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.24,
          "end": 80.61,
          "en": "because in development mode,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.61,
          "end": 84.21000000000001,
          "en": "this code that's being served is not optimized.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.21000000000001,
          "end": 88.5,
          "en": "It's not optimized for size, so it's too big",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.5,
          "end": 93.27000000000001,
          "en": "and it contains some extra logging and error messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.27000000000001,
          "end": 97.08,
          "en": "or error details if errors occur,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.08,
          "end": 99.93,
          "en": "which you also might not want to share",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.93,
          "end": 102.47999999999999,
          "en": "with the entire world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.47999999999999,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "And therefore this development server, as its name suggests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 109.533,
          "en": "is great for development but not for deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.55,
          "end": 113.91,
          "en": "So therefore, we finished this first step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.91,
          "end": 118.8,
          "en": "but now we must prepare this application for deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.8,
          "end": 122.1,
          "en": "And that means that we need to build it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.1,
          "end": 127.1,
          "en": "We must tell Angular or the Angular CLI to be precise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 130.05,
          "en": "that we now want to compile",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.05,
          "end": 133.803,
          "en": "and optimize our code for deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.06,
          "end": 136.82999999999998,
          "en": "When running npm start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.82999999999998,
          "end": 141.69,
          "en": "we actually also tell the Angular CLI to compile our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.69,
          "end": 144.51,
          "en": "because this development server in the end serves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.51,
          "end": 148.07999999999998,
          "en": "the compiled code, but it's not optimized yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.07999999999998,
          "end": 151.87,
          "en": "So now we need compilation and optimization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.73,
          "end": 156.48,
          "en": "and that can be done by running ng build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.48,
          "end": 158.46,
          "en": "or npm run build,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.46,
          "end": 162.84300000000002,
          "en": "which will trigger ng build under the hood, as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.34,
          "end": 168.15,
          "en": "And what this will do is just as during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.15,
          "end": 171.75,
          "en": "it will compile the TypeScript code to JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.75,
          "end": 174.66,
          "en": "since TypeScript doesn't run in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.66,
          "end": 178.56,
          "en": "but it will now also optimize the code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.56,
          "end": 182.46,
          "en": "it will shrink it, make it as small as possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.46,
          "end": 187.443,
          "en": "and overall try to produce an optimized bundle size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 188.73,
          "end": 191.04,
          "en": "And once this process finished,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 191.04,
          "end": 194.31,
          "en": "you should therefore find a dist folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 194.31,
          "end": 196.56,
          "en": "in your project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.56,
          "end": 200.73,
          "en": "And this dist folder should then contain a sub folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 200.73,
          "end": 203.01,
          "en": "that carries your project name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.01,
          "end": 204.96,
          "en": "In my case, simply routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.96,
          "end": 207.963,
          "en": "That's how I named my project when I created it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 209.01,
          "end": 212.64,
          "en": "And that routing folder then contains the folders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.64,
          "end": 215.763,
          "en": "and files that you would deploy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 216.66,
          "end": 218.16,
          "en": "And by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.16,
          "end": 222.573,
          "en": "that folder therefore should contain a browser folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 223.82999999999998,
          "end": 227.19,
          "en": "Now, if you are creating a new Angular project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 227.19,
          "end": 228.45,
          "en": "and you are building that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228.45,
          "end": 232.02,
          "en": "you might actually also have more folders in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 232.02,
          "end": 234.03,
          "en": "a server folder for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.03,
          "end": 236.76,
          "en": "But this project here on which we worked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 236.76,
          "end": 241.113,
          "en": "throughout this course should only have that browser folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.4,
          "end": 244.74,
          "en": "and that folder contains the files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.74,
          "end": 249.39,
          "en": "and folders you would now put on some web host",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.39,
          "end": 254.39,
          "en": "so that these files are exposed to the worldwide web,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 254.4,
          "end": 257.04,
          "en": "and then users could go ahead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 257.04,
          "end": 259.44,
          "en": "and send requests to that web host",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 259.44,
          "end": 263.25,
          "en": "and visit your Angular driven website therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 263.25,
          "end": 264.72,
          "en": "that's in a nutshell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 264.72,
          "end": 267.48,
          "en": "how you can build your application for deployment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 267.48,
          "end": 269.85,
          "en": "and how you could then deploy it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 269.85,
          "end": 272.61,
          "en": "Though I'll show you a practical example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 272.61,
          "end": 274.053,
          "en": "in a couple of minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.89,
          "end": 279.15,
          "en": "But first, let's understand which kind of build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.15,
          "end": 280.40999999999997,
          "en": "we started here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 280.40999999999997,
          "end": 283.92,
          "en": "and which kind of application we built here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 283.92,
          "end": 286.08,
          "en": "Because as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 286.08,
          "end": 289.62,
          "en": "there seemed to be multiple build options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.62,
          "end": 292.02,
          "en": "when building an Angular project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.02,
          "end": 294.543,
          "en": "So which one did we use here?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
